From c2b367449390f40c18e218a921efda35856aede8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <Github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 11:12:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Implement the legacy wakeLockRegister/setWakeLock API

Open webOS clients hold the system awake around active work with the
powerd-era pair

    wakeLockRegister {"register": true, "clientId": "<id>"}
    setWakeLock      {"clientId": "<id>", "isWakeup": true|false}

on /com/palm/power - luna-downloadmgr does exactly this around running
downloads. The methods never existed in the OSE sleepd (its api.json
listed them until 2024, when they were removed as unused), so every
call failed with LS_NO_METH and the client silently lost its ability to
keep the device from suspending mid-download.

Back them with named kernel wakelocks, the same mechanism the activity
timeouts already use: while /sys/power/wake_lock holds webos-<clientId>
the kernel refuses to autosleep, so the veto works against the actual
suspend mechanism rather than sleepd's bookkeeping. Registrations are
also added to a server-side subscription list so clientCancel() fires
when the caller drops off the bus and a crashed client cannot leak its
wakelock until reboot.
---
